# ── Client data — NEVER tracked ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The full 48-report working set is a real client's sealed AISC 360-16
# calculations. Only the sanitized samples in tests/HTMLFilesToBeCompiled/ are
# committed (see scripts/sanitize-report.ts for exactly what is scrubbed).
#
# An entire ignored directory is deliberate: a per-file rule leaks the moment
# someone drops a new report in beside the samples. Keep the real set here and
# build it with `cd local && bun ../main.ts` — the defaults resolve from the
# working directory, so that just works.
/local/

# Private memory: the workspace rules put machine facts (paths, environment notes)
# in a git-ignored `cmem/local/`. `/local/` above covers the top-level folder only,
# so without this a session following that rule here would stage them.
/cmem/local/

# Claude Code project instructions — machine-local, same convention as wasmtk.
# The durable project rules live in cmem/, which IS tracked.
CLAUDE.md

# Claude Code machine-local settings (per-developer permission allowlist).
# It records commands approved on THIS machine and must not travel with the
# repo — an allowlist from one machine should never pre-approve commands on
# someone else's checkout.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Session transcripts. Untracked by owner decision: they carry absolute paths
# from the machine they were recorded on and client identifiers from the report
# excerpts. cmem/*.md is the portable record; the transcripts are not.
/cmem/transcript/

# ── Dependencies ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Node and Bun need these on disk; Deno uses the same folder via
# "nodeModulesDir": "manual" in jsr.json (deno.json until 2026-10-28).
/node_modules

# The npm copy, built by `bun run npm:build` (roadmap task 15) — generated, never committed.
/dist/

# ── Build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Not anchored, and no placeholder is committed: the build creates its output
# directory next to whatever it is compiling, so one appears wherever you run.
#
# No exceptions under this rule. Any PDF produced from the real report set is a
# render of client calculations carrying the same metadata the sample sanitizer
# exists to remove — that is why the Bluebeam benchmark was deleted rather than
# re-included. See cmem/roadmap.md task 3b.
CompiledPDF/

# A SkyCiv zip build (2026-11-06) writes BESIDE the zip, in no output folder: the baked HTML
# (<zip>.html -- every report's full content), the PDF while unverified or not yet in the zip, and
# the partial zip. All client data. Anything of those kinds is ignored everywhere, and the only
# committed HTML -- the sanitized samples and the browser example -- is let back in by name, so a
# report or a bake dropped anywhere else can never be staged (review 2, group C).
*.zip
*.zip.partial
*.pdf
*.html
!/tests/HTMLFilesToBeCompiled/*.html
!/tests/browser_example.html

# Generated browser bundle — rebuild with `bun run bundle:browser`
/tests/report_core.browser.js

# Font cache, populated on first run so later builds work offline. Not anchored
# to the root: it is created in the working directory, so running the build from
# tests/ or local/ drops one there too.
.mathjax-fonts/

# ── Editors / OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
